### Commands that run git itself.

## The commands: what the palette and the command line call each, and what it does.

git-info = Git executable
git-info-description = Which git is run (the one shipped with the application where PATH has none), its version, whether it is new enough and what an older one does without; params: program (ask this executable instead of the one in use)
git-use = Use another git executable
git-use-description = Run this executable as git from now on, in every repository; params: program (a name on PATH or a path; absent or empty for the default), verify (bool, default true: refuse what does not answer as git)
